Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `channelGrouping` : traffic source category; will be used to group sessions/transactions  
• `geoNetwork_country` : visitor’s country; used to segment totals per country  
• `totals_transactions` : number of transactions that happened in a hit / visit; summed to obtain the total per country & channel grouping  
• `fullVisitorId`, `visitId` : visit identifiers that allow us to keep only one copy of each visit when de‑duplicating  
• (optional) `hits_transaction_transactionRevenue` / `totals_totalTransactionRevenue` : monetary value, not required here but sometimes helpful in sanity checks  
Conditions that may be useful  
• `totals_transactions IS NOT NULL`  – keep rows where at least one transaction took place  
• `COUNT(DISTINCT geoNetwork_country) > 1` – retain only those channel groupings that appear in more than one country  
• Use `SELECT DISTINCT …` or `QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (…) = 1` to eliminate duplicate rows first  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final BigQuery SQL queries.  
Each query is written against the public table  
`data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`  
(remember to enclose identifiers in back‑ticks).

```sql
-- 1️⃣ Description: show every distinct channel grouping that records at
-- least one row in the transactions table.
SELECT DISTINCT `channelGrouping`
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2️⃣ Description: list some distinct countries that have any
-- transactions recorded.
SELECT DISTINCT `geoNetwork_country`
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
WHERE `totals_transactions` IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3️⃣ Description: simple aggregation – total transactions by channel
-- and country (ignores duplicates for the moment).
SELECT
  `channelGrouping`,
  `geoNetwork_country` AS country,
  SUM(`totals_transactions`) AS sum_transactions
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
WHERE `totals_transactions` IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY 1,2
ORDER BY 1,3 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4️⃣ Description: count how many different countries contribute at
-- least one transaction within each channel grouping (duplicates not
-- yet handled).
SELECT
  `channelGrouping`,
  COUNT(DISTINCT `geoNetwork_country`) AS countries_with_tx
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
WHERE `totals_transactions` IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY 1
ORDER BY countries_with_tx DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5️⃣ Description: isolate channel groupings that register transactions
-- in more than one country (still ignoring duplicates).
SELECT
  `channelGrouping`
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
WHERE `totals_transactions` IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY `channelGrouping`
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT `geoNetwork_country`) > 1;
```

```sql
-- 6️⃣ Description: inspect the raw data for possible duplication by
-- checking how often the same (fullVisitorId, visitId) pair appears.
SELECT
  COUNT(*) AS rows_in_table,
  COUNT(DISTINCT STRUCT(`fullVisitorId`, `visitId`)) AS distinct_visits
FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`;
```

```sql
-- 7️⃣ Description: create a de‑duplicated temporary table that keeps
-- only one record per visit (fullVisitorId + visitId).
WITH dedup AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT
    `fullVisitorId`,
    `visitId`,
    `channelGrouping`,
    `geoNetwork_country`,
    `totals_transactions`
  FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
)
SELECT * FROM dedup LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8️⃣ Description: after de‑duplication, aggregate transactions for
-- every (channel, country) pair.
WITH dedup AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT
    `fullVisitorId`,
    `visitId`,
    `channelGrouping`,
    `geoNetwork_country`,
    `totals_transactions`
  FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
)
SELECT
  `channelGrouping`,
  `geoNetwork_country` AS country,
  SUM(`totals_transactions`) AS sum_transactions
FROM dedup
WHERE `totals_transactions` IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY 1,2
ORDER BY 1,3 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9️⃣ Description: for every channel that spans multiple countries,
-- pick the country with the largest summed transactions using
-- QUALIFY + window functions.
WITH dedup AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT
    `fullVisitorId`,
    `visitId`,
    `channelGrouping`,
    `geoNetwork_country`,
    `totals_transactions`
  FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
),
agg AS (
  SELECT
    `channelGrouping`,
    `geoNetwork_country`   AS country,
    SUM(`totals_transactions`) AS sum_transactions,
    COUNT(DISTINCT `geoNetwork_country`) OVER (PARTITION BY `channelGrouping`) AS country_count
  FROM dedup
  WHERE `totals_transactions` IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY 1,2
)
SELECT
  `channelGrouping`,
  country,
  sum_transactions
FROM agg
WHERE country_count > 1
QUALIFY ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY `channelGrouping`
                           ORDER BY sum_transactions DESC) = 1
ORDER BY `channelGrouping`;
```

```sql
-- 🔟 Description (final answer): same result as #9 but written with
-- ARRAY_AGG for variety; returns each channel grouping, the top country
-- by total transactions, and that total (duplicates already removed).
WITH dedup AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT
    `fullVisitorId`,
    `visitId`,
    `channelGrouping`,
    `geoNetwork_country`,
    `totals_transactions`
  FROM `data-to-insights.ecommerce.rev_transactions`
),
tx_by_country AS (
  SELECT
    `channelGrouping`,
    `geoNetwork_country`  AS country,
    SUM(`totals_transactions`) AS total_tx
  FROM dedup
  WHERE `totals_transactions` IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY 1,2
),
top_per_channel AS (
  SELECT
    `channelGrouping`,
    ARRAY_AGG(
      STRUCT(country, total_tx) ORDER BY total_tx DESC
    )[SAFE_OFFSET(0)] AS best
  FROM tx_by_country
  GROUP BY `channelGrouping`
  HAVING COUNT(*) > 1   -- only keep channels present in >1 country
)
SELECT
  `channelGrouping`,
  best.country          AS top_country,
  best.total_tx         AS sum_transactions
FROM top_per_channel
ORDER BY `channelGrouping`;
```

These ten queries take you from a quick look at the data all the way to the fully de‑duplicated answer required in the task.
